  "description": {
    "text": "The eight foil Energy cards of the 2002 Pokémon TCG League, the third year of Wizards of the Coast's League, which ran from 6 January to October 2002 and was known as the \"Energize Your Game\" League after them. Wizards brought tournaments into the League that year: each of its eight seasons ended with a tournament open to every League member, and playing in it earned that season's foil Energy, a kind of promo Wizards said it had never released before. The season's winners received extra copies.\n\nThey are unnumbered foil prints of existing Energy cards, with no black star promo mark: Rainbow Energy for the first season, then Fighting, Fire, Grass, Lightning, Psychic and Water Energy, and Recycle Energy for the eighth and last, in September 2002. Rainbow Energy already had a holo print in Team Rocket, so its promo has the foil over the whole card.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Wizards of the Coast: Pokémon TCG League: What's New in 2002? (Wayback Machine copy, 2 February 2002)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20020202083751/http://www.wizards.com/default.asp?x=pokemon/league/year3Intro"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Wizards Pokemon League Year 3: Energize Your Game",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/wizards-pokemon-league-year-3-energize-your-game/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Pokémon League Rewards (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 22 June 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260622235759/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_League_Rewards_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Recycle Energy (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 6 March 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260306071153/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Recycle_Energy_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
